message.content:
Use the CSS **`:hover`** pseudo-class on the `span` itself; it works on any element, not just links.[4][8]

```html
<span class="my-span">Hover me</span>
```

```css
.my-span {
  color: black;
}

.my-span:hover {
  color: red;
}
```

If the span already has inline styles or stronger rules, the hover rule may be overridden; in that case, remove the inline styling or increase specificity as needed.[1][4]

If you want, I can also show the version for changing the color of a parent element when the span is hovered.

